# Tools the repo's own tooling shells out to. Every entry is justified by a real
# call site. This file is data: one tool per line, blank lines and whole-line
# `#` comments ignored, no shebang and no executable bit.
#
# A `#` comment on the SAME line as a tool is NOT a free-form note -- it is an
# annotation the lint reads and validates. Exactly one annotation exists:
#
#   kcov  # linux-only
#
# `linux-only` means the devShell carries the tool on Linux and deliberately
# does not carry it elsewhere, so the forward pass skips the entry (loudly, with
# a SKIP: line) when it is not running on Linux. Anything else after the `#` on
# a tool's line is a hard failure, not a comment: a typo'd `# linux_only` that
# quietly reverted to "required on every platform" is exactly the drift this
# file exists to catch. Put a justifying note on its own line ABOVE the tool,
# the way every entry below already does.
#
# .ci/check-devshell-provides reads this file in both directions:
# - forward: every entry here must resolve on PATH inside the devShell;
# - reverse: every devShell package must be where one of these binaries actually
#   RESOLVES on PATH, OR back a formatter .treefmt.nix enables. Resolution, not
#   mere presence: a package shipping a binary that another package shadows is
#   contributing nothing to the shell, and the lint says so.
#
# That second escape is why prettier, yamlfmt, nixfmt and taplo are absent:
# treefmt runs them from the Nix store, never through PATH, and the lint derives
# their exemption from .treefmt.nix rather than from a list kept here.

# invoked by .ci/run-lint-checks
actionlint
# run-tests invokes bats from PATH; the devShell provides it
bats
# invoked by .githooks/commit-msg
commitlint
# invoked by .ci/run-lint-checks
editorconfig-checker
# invoked by .ci/run-lint-checks
deadnix
# invoked by .ci/run-lint-checks
statix
# the hook's own runtime dependency, scanner.bats drives it directly, and
# .ci/run-lint-checks lints the scanner with `gawk --lint=fatal --posix`
gawk
# one-true-awk (BWK); run-tests --awk=bwk shims `awk` to it
nawk
# asserted by .ci/check-uses-sha-pinned and used by the release flow
gh
# every repo-tooling script derives the repo root via `git rev-parse`
git
# the hook's own runtime dependency; manifest.bats parses JSON with it
jq
# the task runner the .justfile and README document
just
# invoked by `run-tests --coverage`, which `just coverage` drives, to measure
# the hook's line coverage under the bats suite. nixpkgs' kcov declares no
# darwin platform at all, so flake.nix adds it behind `lib.optionals
# stdenv.isLinux` and the forward pass must skip it off Linux rather than
# report a missing tool the shell was never going to have (#91).
kcov  # linux-only
# invoked by .ci/check-links
lychee
# invoked by .ci/run-lint-checks
markdownlint-cli2
# the gates' own nix; flake.nix pins it as nix.out so this resolves to the
# locked 2.34.8 rather than to whatever nix the host happens to ship
nix
# invoked by .ci/run-lint-checks; the binary name, not its `renovate` package
renovate-config-validator
# the lint gate for the repo's entire payload
shellcheck
# the format gate; treefmt drives it, check-scripts verifies it
shfmt
# invoked by .ci/run-lint-checks
typos
# invoked by .ci/run-lint-checks
yamllint
# invoked by .ci/run-lint-checks; the workflow security audit next to actionlint
zizmor
# invoked by .ci/check-issue-forms
yq

# The baseline userland the gates shell out to. stdenv puts these on PATH
# anyway, at byte-identical store paths, so naming them buys no new binary --
# it converts an inherited nixpkgs internal (stdenv.initialPath, which no gate
# asserts and a flake.lock bump could change) into a declared dependency, and
# it is what justifies coreutils, findutils and gnugrep to the reverse pass.
# invoked by .ci/check-err-trap-hygiene, .ci/check-versions-in-sync and
# .ci/check-issue-forms
grep
# tests/repeat.bats walks the state dir with it
find
# bench/run creates its sample directories with it
mkdir
